<!-- Actual RV64 instruction encodings, lifted through the real language.
     The gcc model declares ra as returnaddress.
     Each final 0x8082 is the compressed return: its real Sleigh lowering is
     RETURN[ra], unlike the uncompressed return's low-bit masking operation.
     This isolates COPY-use safety, not tagged-return arithmetic or reverse
     candidate enumeration (the compressed RETURN names ra directly).

     return_copy: mv t1,ra; mv ra,t1; c.ret
     partial_read: sw ra,0(a3); c.ret
     narrowed_target: sext.w t1,ra; mv ra,t1; c.ret
     output_escape: mv a0,ra; c.ret
     implicit_parent: mv t1,ra; mv a2,ra; jal ra,consume_a2;
                      mv ra,t1; c.ret
     consume_a2: sd a2,0(a3); li a0,0; c.ret
     The JAL at 0x1408 targets the actual body at 0x1500. Adjacent a2 and a3
     input reads may be coalesced: tests require byte containment, not a
     particular range packaging. No source declarations alter machine facts. -->
